          <p style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:12px;">Unconscious bias can affect hiring decisions without us even realising it. Look at the five scenarios below. Which ones might introduce bias into an interview? How could an interviewer counteract each one?</p>
          <ol style="font-size:14px;line-height:2;padding-left:20px;">
            <li>The candidate attended the same university as you and you immediately feel a connection.</li>
            <li>The candidate has a strong accent that is unfamiliar to you and you have to concentrate harder to understand them.</li>
            <li>The candidate's CV has a two-year gap that they explained was for family caregiving reasons.</li>
            <li>The candidate is much younger than you expected for a senior role.</li>
            <li>The candidate is dressed very casually for the interview.</li>
          </ol>
